[{"category":"section","location":"#SingularIntegrals.jl","page":"Home","text":"A Julia package for computing singular integrals involving Hilbert/Stieltjes/Cauchy, log, and power law kernels.","title":"SingularIntegrals.jl"},{"category":"section","location":"#Examples","page":"Home","text":"Expand exp(x) in Legendre polynomials and compute singular integrals against it:\n\njulia> using SingularIntegrals, ClassicalOrthogonalPolynomials\njulia> P = Legendre(); x = axes(P, 1); f = expand(P, exp);\njulia> inv.(10 .- x') * f # Stieltjes: ∫₋₁¹ exp(x) / (10-x) dx\n0.24332755428373515\njulia> inv.(0.1+0im .- x') * f - inv.(0.1-0im .- x') * f ≈ -2π*im*exp(0.1) # example of Plemelj\ntrue\n\nPower law kernels are supported for Legendre and weighted ultraspherical bases:\n\njulia> (abs.(10 .- x') .^ 0.2 * Legendre())[1:5] # ∫₋₁¹ (10-x)^0.2 * P_k(x) dx for k = 0,…,4\n5-element Vector{Float64}:\n  3.1689389691547674\n -0.021162455415691145\n -0.00033933394993157853\n -8.74599143396353e-6\n -2.727481731934075e-7\n\nLog kernels are supported for weighted bases:\n\njulia> W = Weighted(ChebyshevU()); f = expand(W, x -> exp(x) * sqrt(1-x^2));\njulia> log.(abs.(10 .- x')) * f # Log-kernel: ∫₋₁¹ log(10-x) * exp(x) * sqrt(1-x^2) dx\n4.043032838853287\njulia> log.(abs.(0.3 .- x')) * f # ∫₋₁¹ log(abs(0.3-x)) * exp(x) * sqrt(1-x^2) dx\n-2.3203915590084447","title":"Examples"},{"category":"section","location":"#API","page":"Home","text":"","title":"API"},{"category":"type","location":"#SingularIntegrals.AssociatedWeight","page":"Home","text":"AssociatedWeighted(P)\n\nWe normalise so that orthogonalityweight(::Associated) is a probability measure.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"SingularIntegrals.AssociatedWeight"},{"category":"method","location":"#SingularIntegrals.cauchy-Tuple{Any, Vararg{Any}}","page":"Home","text":"cauchy(P, z)\n\ncomputes inv.(t'-z) * P/(2π*im) where t = axes(P,1).\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"SingularIntegrals.cauchy"},{"category":"method","location":"#SingularIntegrals.complexlogkernel-Tuple{Any, Vararg{Any}}","page":"Home","text":"complexlogkernel(P)\n\napplies the log kernel log(x-t) to the columns of a quasi matrix, i.e., (log.(x - x') * P)\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"SingularIntegrals.complexlogkernel"},{"category":"method","location":"#SingularIntegrals.hilbert-Tuple{Any, Vararg{Any}}","page":"Home","text":"hilbert(P, x)\n\ncomputes inv.(x - t') * P/π in a principle value sense where t = axes(P,1) and x in t.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"SingularIntegrals.hilbert"},{"category":"method","location":"#SingularIntegrals.hilbert-Union{Tuple{ClassicalOrthogonalPolynomials.ChebyshevTWeight{T}}, Tuple{T}} where T","page":"Home","text":"hilbert(P)\n\ncomputes (inv.(x - x') * P)/π understood in a principle value sense.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"SingularIntegrals.hilbert"},{"category":"method","location":"#SingularIntegrals.logkernel-Tuple{Any, Vararg{Any}}","page":"Home","text":"logkernel(P)\n\napplies the log kernel log(abs(x-t)) to the columns of a quasi matrix, i.e., (log.(abs.(x - x')) * P)\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"SingularIntegrals.logkernel"},{"category":"method","location":"#SingularIntegrals.stieltjes-Tuple{Any, Vararg{Any}}","page":"Home","text":"stieltjes(P, z)\n\ncomputes inv.(z - t') * P where t = axes(P,1).\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"SingularIntegrals.stieltjes"}]
